    "created_at": "2023-01-05T19:20:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-01-05T19:20:01Z",
    "body": "Hmm good point. Thinking about this a bit more.... Writes using any storage API (including this one) can be rejected if the site is out of quota. So do all storage APIs need to use same task source for writes, since [they all interact with the Quota Management API](https://www.w3.org/TR/quota-api/#accessing-storagequota-interface)?\r\n\r\nThere are a couple of other [[1](https://www.w3.org/TR/IndexedDB/#request-source), [2](https://www.w3.org/TR/FileAPI/#blobreader-task-source)] storage-related task sources that I'm aware of, but they both queue operations that are read-only (i.e. don't affect quota)",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/fs/issues/comments/1372631756/reactions",
