    "updated_at": "2023-01-06T09:30:47Z",
    "body": "That's a good point too.\r\n\r\nSo, the tasks are for informing the event loop about the result of a storage operation. So yes, write storage operations need to be in order (at least per site), but reporting whether that succeeded or not back to JavaScript (this involves tasks) doesn't necessarily have to be in the same order, but we might as well stick to a single task source for that I think.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
